.TH "PB-SEND-DESTINATION-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-send-destination-set - Set the default transfer destination


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb send destination set <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the default transfer destination

.PP
Save one enrolled machine as the default recipient for future sends. A command's explicit --to selection takes precedence over this local default.

.PP
Send publishes a batch to a machine's Paperboat Inbox. Completion means the receiver verified and recorded the files; status and cancel act on a transfer ID. A default destination can be set separately, while --to chooses one for the current send.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	terminal session ID for a session-specific destination

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-send-destination(1)\fP
